{
  "description": "The one table that turns an `XCUIElement.ElementType` raw value into the `type` name an iOS snapshot publishes (issue #4657). Both iOS producers read it: the Simulator AX bridge names every entry by index in `ELEMENT_TYPE_NAMES` in packages/platform-apple/src/snapshot-source/tree.ts, and the XCTest runner mirrors every entry by raw value in `elementTypeNamesByRawValue` in apple/runner/AgentDeviceRunner/AgentDeviceRunnerUITests/RunnerTests+Snapshot.swift. One node captured twice, once per producer, must carry one name: a consumer that keys on `type` cannot know which producer served a capture, because the backend is chosen per capture. `sdkCase` names the SDK case that carries a row's `rawValue`, so the runner's parity test compares the row with that case and an SDK renumbering fails against the SDK; a null `sdkCase` names a value the SDK hides from Swift, which both producers still publish. A row reaches a snapshot by its name on both producers. What a producer does with a raw value no row names is its own: the runner spells it `unnamedTypeSpelling` and the bridge reports `Other`, and the presented-surface rule reads either spelling by number (#3565).",
